WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.650
Everyone, when you're watching Deltora Quest,

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:09.300
make sure you're in a well-lit
room and sit far away from the TV!

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:24.040
You are my sun now

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.460
We all go through bad times

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.460
no matter who you are

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.890
So don't go hanging your head and feeling down

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:45.600
Keep your head up until your heart's sky

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.980
is clear again

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:56.360
No matter where you are in this world

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:59.870
if you're crying and trembling all alone

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:05.210
I'll search for you, I promise

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.880
Love will show me the way

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:16.720
The sun dreams countless times

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:23.520
Forever and always from the horizon

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:30.900
Its shining light gives energy

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:38.240
After all, you are my sun now

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.580
<i>All seven gems have been retrieved.</i>

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:02.300
<i>But, that is not enough to defeat the Shadow Lord.</i>

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.960
<i>Now they must find the heir to the throne.</i>

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:24.580
This list that Lief just made shows all of the gems,
the tribes from which they all come,

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:29.700
as well as the names of proposed
representatives from each of those tribes.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.400
Lief, read it aloud.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.200
Sure.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:38.750
Topaz: The Del tribe.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.000
Barda.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.500
By the way, Lief is also from Del tribe.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.750
Ruby: The Ralad tribe.

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:48.100
Manus.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.470
Opal: The Plains tribe.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.100
Steven and Nevets.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:56.700
Huh?!

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:59.300
Steven aside, Nevets can't
possibly be a representative!

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.300
You should know this already from last night...

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.520
Shh! Just listen.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.770
Lapis lazuli: The Mere tribe.

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:08.100
Fardeep.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:13.900
Picking someone like me as a representative is quite bizarre, but I will accept!

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:17.120
Emerald: The Dread Gnome tribe.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:18.300
Gla-Thon.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.830
Amethyst: The Toran tribe.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.000
Zeean.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:27.090
On the honour of the Torans!

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:30.300
Diamond: The Jalis tribe.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:31.600
Glock.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.500
Huh? Glock?!

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.600
Shh!

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:37.900
We will gather these seven together.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.500
Why is Glock of all people on the list?

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:47.600
This entire area used to be
inhabited by the Jalis tribe.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:52.100
They were a group of excellent
warriors with fiery tempers.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:56.000
But, in spite of their strength,
they suffered an ill fate.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:01.200
The Jalis tribe was utterly
destroyed by the Shadow Lord.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:07.600
Miraculously, Glock survived and became the
only remaining member of his kind.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.200
We have no other option.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:13.600
If we invite that man to our gathering,
his behaviour will only throw everything into chaos.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:15.800
If this Glock person is the last of his kind,

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:20.390
then we have no choice but to let him in,
regardless of what kind of man he may be.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:28.400
Of those seven, the only ones who aren't here at this
moment are Manus, Gla-Thon, and Glock, correct?

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:32.400
We'll have to contact them
and tell them to come here.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:38.200
How are we going to send messages to places like
The Forests of Silence and The Lake of Tears?

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:43.450
Oh right! Kree can just fly there!

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.700
We can also use my contacts in the Resistance.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:53.300
I'm honoured to have the opportunity to host
this meeting between the seven tribes.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.900
Well, regarding that,

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:59.800
if we're found out by the Grey Guards,
they'll have us like a rat in a bag.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.560
I know a place to hide.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:07.800
It's safe and in good order. There is no better hiding place than this one.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.600
And where exactly is it?

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.500
It's close to the city of Del,
in a place called Withick Mire.

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.700
In fact, Glock is hiding there as well.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.800
I don't want go to where Glock is!

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.600
That's enough, Jasmine.

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:28.700
If it's close to Del, then I feel that it will be
a convenient location, given our future plans.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:32.900
But, wouldn't such place be under heavy
surveillance by Grey Guards?

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:37.090
Indeed, it is. But they also won't
be expecting us to be there.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:44.200
If there are no objections, then the gathering of
the seven tribes shall be held in Withick Mire.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.600
Very well. I will make
arrangements immediately.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:48.890
Let us help you with that.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.100
Kree, can you do this?

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:01.670
"Leave it to me!", he says.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:09.000
Take this to Gla-Thon in Dread Mountain,
and take care not to drop it.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.150
Now, tell this to everyone.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:27.500
I'm counting on you.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:34.600
With this, the news should spread all
across the land within a few days.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.200
By the way, Steven.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.500
I need to ask one more thing of you.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:43.990
Of course, anything I can do to help.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:48.500
Me, representing the Plains tribe?

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:52.900
I-I-I couldn't do that!
I'm just a travelling merchant!

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:56.450
Please, you must find someone
more suitable than myself!

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:59.300
Then who <i>would</i> be more suitable than you?

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:02.500
We don't know anyone else from the Plains tribe.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:07.300
Please wait for a moment. I need to
discuss this with my brother first...

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:12.400
That's right... they said I should
represent the Plains tribe...

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:15.600
Then I really should just accept...

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:18.400
Ah, but I'm worried about...

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:20.100
Yeah, that...

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:29.800
As much as I'd like to accept,
there is one big problem...

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.300
It's my older brother, Nevets.

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:34.100
Your brother?

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:40.000
Bad things will happen if my brother
comes out. Is that really fine with you?

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:46.500
But we have no other people from
the Plains tribe except you here.

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:51.400
I beg you, please do this, for
the new Kingdom of Deltora.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:55.300
In that case, I will accept.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:58.700
Okay. Let's go to Withick Mire.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:02.250
If we all go together, the enemy
will find us with ease.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:04.400
Let us split into two groups.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:09.500
This particularly applies to Lief's group who are
already being pursued by the Grey Guards.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.200
Shall we hide you inside Steven's wagon?

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:12.950
Huh?

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:15.900
Does that mean that we won't have to walk?

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:17.300
That sounds great!

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:28.390
It may be a little bit cramped,
but please bear with it.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:32.750
Really? In this cramped space?

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:35.100
Maybe walking <i>would</i> be better...

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:39.900
I'm sorry. It is necessary to hide
you from the Grey Guards.

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:41.700
Ah, I'm sorry.

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.530
I wasn't complaining about you or anything.

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:50.600
Barda, Jasmine. Look over there.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:59.100
This journey may be dangerous,

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:02.600
but it is also a very important duty.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:04.260
I entrust this task to you.

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:06.260
Leave it to us.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.180
Please wait!

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:12.300
Where are those three going?

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.700
We're heading to the River Tor.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:16.700
For what purpose?!

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:21.600
Could it be... that you're going
to be our body doubles?

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:24.100
Don't do it! It's far too dangerous!

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:26.610
We are well aware of the dangers.

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:32.400
This is a necessary step in ensuring our success.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.700
As well as that...

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:39.800
As Torans, this is the perfect
opportunity to redeem ourselves.

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:42.090
Please, allow us to do this.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:55.900
Is this really okay?

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:58.800
What would you do in their position?

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:02.800
I would probably become
a body double and go as well.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:04.110
Me too.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:05.500
Exactly.

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:12.100
That is why we must fulfill
our duties without fail.

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:12.700
Yeah.

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:13.800
I guess so.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:17.400
Now then, shall we begin our journey too?

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:18.100
Yeah.

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:18.790
Okay.

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:28.500
You must reach Withick Mire no matter what.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:29.900
Promise me that.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.400
And you as well!

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.470
Be careful, you three.

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:37.600
I have your good luck charm.

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:39.400
You be careful too, Dain.

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:41.000
Just Dain?

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:42.800
Everyone but you!

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:45.900
It would appear that I am thoroughly hated.

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:49.100
Wait, Doom!

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:53.400
Um... about last night...

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:56.740
Thank you for saving me...

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.300
What was that?

00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.620
I can't hear you.

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:02.200
Thank you for last night!

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:05.900
You're welcome.

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:13.600
What's the hell is with his attitude?!

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:16.100
I just went and thanked him and everything!

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:18.500
I really do hate this guy after all!

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:22.310
Alright, it's time to go.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:54.800
We have a message from our friend, Lief!

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:58.800
Their bird Kree flew here
to deliver this message!

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:01.600
I will now translate Kree's words.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:08.400
"We have gathered all of the
seven gems of Deltora."

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:17.600
"But, to unleash the Belt's power,
we need the help of all seven tribes."

00:12:19.150 --> 00:12:24.400
"We want Gla-Thon to represent the Dread Gnome tribe and to meet us at the stronghold in Withick Mire."

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:29.450
"In the meeting with representatives of all seven tribes,

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:33.400
we will search for the king's heir, and the fight against the Shadow Lord will begin."

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:38.140
I'll go and tell Mum and the others about this!

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:43.100
So this day has finally come.

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:46.650
Lief, Jasmine, Barda!

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:57.300
"Come alone... to our friends...
hurry up... for freedom."

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:06.300
Everyone, it seems that the seven scattered gems
of the Belt of Deltora have been retrieved!

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:12.000
I'm sure that the fight against the
Shadow Lord will begin soon.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:17.800
I will go as the representative of the Ralads and
pledge fealty to the king of the Belt's choosing.

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:22.200
Lief, Jasmine, Barda...

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:25.100
Wait for me. I'm on my way.

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:35.800
Oh dear,

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:37.700
there's a customer in the shop.

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:39.320
Excuse me for a moment.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.000
Welcome.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:43.700
What do you need?

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:50.300
Ah, the item you ordered has indeed arrived.

00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:52.700
Here it is.

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:55.800
All of the gems have been retrieved.

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:57.000
Really?

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:03.500
Understood. Tell me if you need anything.

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:06.900
Those three...

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.100
They've done it at last, have they?

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:13.600
Things are going to get busy.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:20.100
Enjoy your days of relaxation while you still can.

00:14:29.900 --> 00:14:32.000
He can even sleep here...?

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:33.800
As you'd expect of a former palace guard.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:36.000
He can take a nap at any time.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:38.300
You should sleep too, Jasmine.

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:40.800
I couldn't even if I wanted to.

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:45.900
On top of being cramped in this wagon,
that guy just won't stop singing.

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:49.900
My back, my legs, and even my head hurt.

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:52.940
Well, after listening for a while it is a bit...

00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:55.600
...stop and rest.

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:58.700
Behold, witness this and see.

00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:04.710
There are no Ak-Babas here.
The Ol-ios are gone.

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:05.700
Hey!

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:08.100
We're stopping soon.

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:09.200
Huh?

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:13.000
We'll be able to get off this wagon
and stretch our legs soon.

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:17.600
Our destination is the forest, and there
are no Ols or Ak-Babas in sight.

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:20.200
What are you talking about all of a sudden, Lief?

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:25.200
Jasmine, Steven is describing the
situation outside by singing to us.

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:25.930
Huh?!

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:29.400
Ol-ios, Ol-ios, they have all gone.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:32.600
The road is straight and empty.

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:35.600
Perfect to stop and take a rest.

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:39.000
Oh you soft and flabby little Ol-ios, hey!

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:42.200
Just stay put and be quiet...

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:51.300
Steven, do you know where we are right now?

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:57.000
We are now on the road that
leads directly to the city of Del.

00:15:57.400 --> 00:16:01.600
Withick Mire is just a slight detour from here.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:03.300
We should be there tomorrow.

00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:06.090
Is it really okay to take such a direct path?

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:09.100
Well, that's the plan for now.

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:13.100
From the perspective of our friends,
or rather, the Grey Guards,

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:18.300
they would never expect you
guys to take the direct route.

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:22.000
So we are just one day away from Del, huh?

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:26.870
We're finally so close to home...

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:34.800
The day I return home to Del will be the
day the Shadow Lord is defeated.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.900
I will see us through to that end!

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:06.700
Flee or fight, which one do you choose?

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:09.000
Think hard and well, my Ol-ios.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:09.900
Hey!

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:12.700
To the right are the gripper fields.

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:15.200
Ahead of us are the Grey Guards.

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:16.050
Hey!

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:18.000
A Grey Guard checkpoint?!

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.200
What does he mean by 'gripper fields'?

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:23.100
Ol-ios, Ol-ios, where are you going?

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:26.050
To the left is a cliff we can't pass,

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:29.000
to the right are the gripper fields. Hey!

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:31.900
Where do you want to run to?

00:17:30.100 --> 00:17:31.600
This is bad!

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:35.300
Make haste and decide. Hey!

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.700
Listen, getting away from them is our priority.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:36.100
Don't forget that.

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:49.400
Now listen. I will attract their attention.

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:51.300
Use the opportunity to run away.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:57.120
Now, would you like some Queen Bee Cider?

00:17:57.600 --> 00:17:59.500
It's the real thing!

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:00.600
Hey you!

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:02.800
Don't do your business here!

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:05.700
Well hello there, sir. How about a drink?

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:08.100
I just told you not to do your business here!

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:10.100
Then there's no need to pay.

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:14.500
Let this be free drinks for all
of the Grey Guard gentlemen.

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:17.500
For free? If that's the case, then I'll have some.

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:19.400
Here, it's my pleasure!

00:18:22.900 --> 00:18:24.300
This is good!

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:27.400
It sure is different from the usual stuff.

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:32.500
Too bad, you damned brat.

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:51.300
What is this plant?!

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:54.100
You bastard...!

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:57.100
That's enough!

00:18:59.600 --> 00:19:03.150
Lay down your weapons!
If you don't drop them, he's dead!

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:04.060
Steven...!

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:06.070
We have no choice...

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.100
What about him?

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:15.700
For the crime of trying to help
these fugitives flee, he shall die.

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:16.900
Understood.

00:19:19.850 --> 00:19:21.870
Stop! Please, stop!

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:25.400
Shut up! I'm going to silence you forever!

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:27.400
Stop!!

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:34.840
What?!

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:36.600
What's happening?!

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:42.300
Nevets...

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:55.100
Thank you, Filli.

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:56.750
Jasmine! Hurry!

00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:01.400
Alright!

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:04.500
Don't worry about me! Get out of here!

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:06.150
Stop, Nevets!

00:20:06.150 --> 00:20:07.600
Barda is your ally!

00:20:09.650 --> 00:20:10.400
Lief...!

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:17.760
Barda!

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:24.900
Lief, what do we do?!

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:26.600
We need to calm Nevets down!

00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:27.600
That's impossible!

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:31.730
We have to! From now on, Nevets
is going to be our comrade!

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:33.050
Nevets!

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:37.400
Stop it, Nevets!

00:20:37.400 --> 00:20:40.400
We are your friends! Don't you understand?!

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:44.200
Nevets!

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:50.600
Nevets, listen carefully.

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:54.200
To revive the Kingdom of Deltora,
just like the gems in this belt,

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:57.100
all the seven tribes have to work together!

00:20:57.600 --> 00:21:03.640
<i>At that moment, the amethyst with its
calming power, emitted a strong light.</i>

00:21:05.400 --> 00:21:10.700
I want you and Steven to help me as
representatives of the Plains tribe.

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:12.000
Please!

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:21.800
Lief, watch out! Run!

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:26.200
Nevets, this is the gem of
the Plains tribe, the opal.

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:48.000
N-Nevets...

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:57.800
I wonder if Barda is okay...

00:21:57.800 --> 00:22:01.280
We can treat him once we get to Withick Mire.

00:22:04.900 --> 00:22:06.500
What's this smell?

00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:08.370
It smells like something rotten.

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:12.000
Steven?

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:14.500
Let's keep moving and get out of this place.

00:22:14.500 --> 00:22:16.500
This is bad for Barda's health, too.

00:22:16.500 --> 00:22:18.800
It's just that... this place...

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:22.800
is actually our destination, Withick Mire.

00:22:24.100 --> 00:22:25.200
It can't be!

00:22:25.200 --> 00:22:28.380
Wasn't this supposed to be a safe
place for us to remain hidden?!

00:22:47.550 --> 00:22:53.300
I would be lying to you

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:59.100
if I said I wasn't lonely

00:22:59.850 --> 00:23:05.650
I know I'm not being honest

00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:11.450
but I just can't put it into words

00:23:12.280 --> 00:23:18.450
It's for the sake of our dreams

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:22.000
At this point

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:27.670
to sing "I love you" to a faraway you

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:33.970
my voice would simply fade into the wind

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:40.270
In a way, that's worse than saying "goodbye"

00:23:40.390 --> 00:23:47.400
But someday our dreams will bloom

00:23:47.730 --> 00:23:55.740
Dreams X Dreams

00:24:06.900 --> 00:24:08.000
<i>Nevets.</i>

00:24:09.100 --> 00:24:11.600
<i>The twin brother of Steven
the travelling merchant.</i>

00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:15.300
<i>Normally he hides himself inside Steven,</i>

00:24:15.300 --> 00:24:17.800
<i>but when danger is near,
he will appear in an instant;</i>

00:24:17.800 --> 00:24:19.500
<i>a ferocious giant.</i>

00:24:20.800 --> 00:24:24.500
When we reach our destination,
we reunite with Glock.

00:24:25.300 --> 00:24:27.640
Jasmine, stop fighting with him.

00:24:28.400 --> 00:24:30.500
Then the Carn Unit attacks.

00:24:30.860 --> 00:24:34.740
The Battle of Withick Mire

00:24:31.300 --> 00:24:34.200
Next time, 'The Battle of Withick Mire'.

00:24:49.750 --> 00:24:54.800
See you next time
